.
110526
	read_PTY_pipe:
	replace strlen(buf) to rlen, allow incoming codes \0 to be parsed

	.
	terminal reset properties changed, new CAP :is: code to reset terminal 

	.
	save_keymap to file "%USERPROFILE%\\TinyTerm7.keymap"
	all lines of current keymap will be stored

	load keymap from file "%USERPROFILE%\\TinyTerm7.keymap"
	found lines will be added to current keymap

	TinyTerm7.keymap line format 
	" VK_KEY { \, size \  (size?str:'') }[KEY_MODS] \;\n"
	    "VK_KEY" unsigned in range 0-255
	    "size" unsigned in range 0-32 (strlen(str))
	    	check is only single space between size and str records
		(optional) "str" in binary form [size] chars 

	TinyTerm7.keymap is autoloaded the same as TinyTerm7.cfg

.	
130526
	fix 'term_insert_lines' fail due to active_window added ( win_y+ly was used instead of win_ly )
	
	fix 'LowLevelKeyboardProc' hooked all desktop ( lack if( bFocus) check )

	fix 'clipboard paste' does not follow UTF8/plain8 keyb option 

	better term_SendW, check OEM codepage selected to display option 

	better scanf keymap, use EOF by value:
		//if( fscanf(fi, "%*1[ ]%?c", len, buf ) != 1 ) 

.
180526
	better separated WM_MOUSEMOVE app/term conditions

	changes mouse button up msg always short (only one '\e[Mbxy' msg posted on up event) in any mode,
	so xterm and no_xterm modes will be yet less compatible (reason - real xterm clients anyway can not 
	deal with unknown '\e[Mbxy' msgs)

	add new mouse mode 4 to simplify orig minix 3 commands to 'map mouse to keys'
	in mode 4 
		mouse return only buttons up events without trailing <xy> data 
		for buttons while ctrl key pressed user confirm the app is ready to accept mouse button events
		for wheel ctrl works in reverse way, press ctrl to link mouse to TT7

	changes to minix 3 to mouse M4 mode support 
		'commands/yap/keys.c' pager and man pager
		add to 'char defaultmap[]'
		'bss=^[[Ma:fss=^[[Mb:qui=^[[M2:qui=^X'
		any custom page size can be set by typing number of lines before wheel scroll

		'commands/evi' editor
		add to 'etc/.evirc' 
		'map ^[[Ma visual ^U'
		'map ^[[Mb visual ^D'
		'map ^[[M2 visual :q!^M'
		any custom page size can be set by typing number of lines before wheel scroll

	add new termcap string 'set color attibutes in line' (remote selection support)
#	num of chars; action
#	action: 0 - reverse exising char attr, 1 - use exising bg attr | fg TERM::clr_attr, 
#			2 - use exising fg attr | bg TERM::clr_attr, 3 - use TERM::clr_attr
	':TC=\E[%d;%du:'

	add new termcap string 'set lines color attibutes' (remote selection support)
	':TL=\E[%d;%dU:'

	add new termcap string 'clear %d lines below from cursor_y' (:ce: extention)
	':EL=\E[2;%dK:'

.
270526

	fix :u6: %i - add +1 to cursor_x,y
		int wlen = _snwprintf(wbuf, WBUF_SZ, L"\033[%u;%uR", pt->cursor_y + 1, pt->cursor_x + 1); 

	change less xterm compatible but more robust mouse button bits

		'commands/yap/keys.c' pager and man pager
		change to 'char defaultmap[]'
		'qui=^[[M3'

		'commands/evi' editor
		change to 'etc/.evirc' 
		'map ^[[M3 visual :q!^M'

	terminal mode "output char attributes instead of chars"
	to support app software implemented "insert/delete" terminal commands 
	using local shadow copy of screen
		# set mode
		':As=\E[5h:'
		# reset mode
		':Ae=\E[5l:'
	new TT7 caption mode indicator "b" ("TT7kmuibaT")

	app sofware can not do semantic analyze of patterns like :cm: 
	and needs explicitly added commands to move only along X or Y
	even if the commands are obvious partical :cm: pattern
	otherwise the terminal commands will be software emulated by app
		add	to mx1.cap
		:cb:el:ch:cv:ll:

	add separated fg_COLORS/bg_COLORS RGB fields for the same color idx
	to allow color correction when thin fg color lines agains wide bg color area

.
